== Further Reading and other designs ==
There's a bustling fireworks community online which I had no idea about until I started digging. 

* [http://www.RFRemotech.com/FiringSystems.html www.RFRemotech.com] - This site lists several interesting products and also has a schematic for the diode matrix I used in my design
* [http://www.firingsystems.us/Falcon-II-Fireworks-Igniters-s/52.htm Falcon Ignitors - they changed their design shortly after I bought mine]
* [http://fireworksland.com/forum/index.php Fireworksland forums]
* [http://www.pyrouniverse.com/forum/forum.php Pyro Universe forums]

Something I found out after building this system is that professional firing systems have to ground the ignition wires when not in use to prevent stray RF interference from generating current on the wires and causing accidental ignitions. While the chances are pretty slim that this would happen, it's worth considering in future designs.
